{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-linking-operations","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:linking-operations","kind":"definition","title":"The two geometric linking operations","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-knot-particle-generation"],"tags":["knot","linking","hopf-link","color-tube","exceptional-divisor"],"defines":["linking-operations"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Torsion.LinkingOperation","text":"linking-operations.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/linking-operations.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:linking-operations\"></a><p><strong>Definition.</strong>\n<em>The two <dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-linking-operations\">linking operations</dfn> are the geometric operations that build composite knots from the <a href=\"#def:knot-particle-generation\">torus knot generators</a>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(i)</code> Hopf linking on the exceptional divisor, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(ii)</code> color-tube threading of the color-tube fibration. Together with the generator family <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{G}</code>, they generate the full particle spectrum.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/linking-operations.md","heading":"Definition","number":"9.4.3"}
